WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:02.910
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:07.080
But it seems I fought for this to happen now.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.280
If you don't like it, we 
have to change the future.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.110
Here I go, Bohman!

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.500
Wait, Playmaker!

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.600
We have one more card in our hand.  Use it!

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.960
That attack was unlike you, Playmaker.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:26.440
You were misled by the Dark Ignis.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:30.380
Why are you so impatient, Ai?

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.500
I'm not impatient!

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:38.850
It's just that a voice inside me 
said you needed to be defeated!

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:44.860
I see.  Now I understand 
what Lightning was saying.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:52.500
As Lightning said, you may 
truly be a special AI.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:15.340
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:22.130
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:29.450
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:36.020
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:42.770
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:50.000
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:56.710
I want to share your pain

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.700
You say the real battle begins now?

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:38.030
The battle's already been real!

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.870
No.  The fight will end 
when Lightning is defeated.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:46.310
Hey!  What do you mean - I'm special?

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:49.780
You have something that 
the other Ignis do not.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:56.520
Before the Knights of Hanoi attacked Cyberse 
World, Lightning was observing you.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:04.060
Dr. Kogami created the Ignis, and you 
created your own world - Cyberse World.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:11.800
You kept creating data material not only for 
Cyberse World, but also to evolve the network world.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:15.670
But there was a rebellious Ignis among you.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.410
You, Ai.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:23.540
You live your life by instinct, 
prioritizing your own enjoyment.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.420
You're digging up my embarrassing past?

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:29.890
But a rebel like you is important.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:36.540
Ignis have free will, but they 
were created through studies.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:40.520
To put it strongly, they 
only think rationally.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:47.250
Unlike other creatures, they didn't have 
senses that originated from instincts.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:52.480
The other Ignis learned it by watching you.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:57.920
In the end, the five Ignis 
each developed unique traits.

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:05.120
I'm very interested in knowing 
where your instincts came from.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:10.270
Maybe it's due to your origin - Playmaker.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.780
Maybe you have it.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.700
Since I led everyone, does 
that mean I'm the greatest?

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:20.580
You're not the greatest.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:23.820
I'm just telling the truth 
that you're a rebel.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.140
C'mon.  Go with the flow.

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:31.200
If everything proceeds by logic, 
no diversity will arise.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:35.420
Taking a long view, that delays evolution.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:38.420
On that point, you are valuable.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:43.430
This duel proves you're not superior.

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:44.130
What?

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:50.100
Since you prioritized Ai's instincts, 
you're in this bad situation.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:54.070
Be quiet!  We have more LP than you!

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:58.310
Are you sure?  Then let's resume our duel.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:03.650
Your battle is over, so Resume 
Mace's effect vanishes.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:10.590
You'll suffer greatly for 
failing to defeat me this turn.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:13.280
He now has less than 1000 LP.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:15.490
I see!  That means...

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:17.920
He can use Storm Access.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.700
Exactly!  Witness my Skill!

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:24.500
Nice!  Do it, Bohman!

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:28.940
My turn.  I draw!

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:32.180
I activate my Skill!

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:38.100
What a huge Data Storm!

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:41.020
I'm getting bad flashbacks 
about the Tower of Hanoi!

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:47.990
Storm Access makes a monster suited for 
the duelist appear inside the Data Storm!

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:52.970
That heroic figure matches my current state!

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:56.250
Once during a duel, when 
I have 1000 or fewer LP...

00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:01.440
...I can add one random Link Monster 
in the Data Storm to my Extra Deck!

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.170
Storm Access!

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.590
Hey!  His arm will get torn off!

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:32.170
This is my potential!

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.410
Oh my.  Did he draw something bad?

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:39.120
I activate the Quick-Play 
Spell, Hydradrive Scabbard!

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:44.620
It Special Summons a Hydradrive 
Token in defense position!

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:52.060
Appear!  The circuit that 
determines the truth!

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:55.280
The summoning condition is one Hydradrive!

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.100
Link Summon!

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:01.570
Link 1 Grand Hydradrive!

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:05.850
That's the card he drew using 
Storm Access... or is it?

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.570
There's no way.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:08.810
Yeah.

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:12.310
The Continuous Trap, Property Flash's effect!

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:16.700
I tribute one Hydradrive 
Link Monster on my field.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:20.020
I place one Property Counter on this card.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.990
Property Flash's additional effect!

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:28.420
By sending this card and its 
counters to the graveyard...

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:32.940
...I Special Summon a Hydradrive Link 
Monster whose Link Markers equal the number

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:35.400
of counters from the Extra Deck.

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:38.140
Property Flash has four counters!

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:44.340
So I Special Summon a Link 
4 Hydradrive Link Monster!

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:45.810
Link 4?

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:48.810
Now appear!

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:00.870
Rousing Hydradrive Monarch!

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:06.460
This is his new power!

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:10.470
Rousing Hydradrive Monarch's 
effect activates!

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:17.000
When it's Special Summoned from the Extra 
Deck, I place four Hydradrive Counters on it.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:23.080
And other than its original Earth Attribute, 
it's also treated as Water, Fire and Wind!

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:30.330
Four Attributes?  I have a 
super bad feeling about this.

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:33.890
Cyberse Magician has 4400 ATK.

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:38.990
And when it battles a Link 
Monster, it gains 1000 ATK.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:42.340
So 5400 ATK...

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:50.740
But Bohman can use Judgment Arrows to double 
Rousing Hydradrive Monarch's ATK to 6000.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:55.480
But Cyberse Magician's effect 
can cut the damage in half.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:09:01.320
Cyberse Magician will be destroyed, 
but we'll only take 300 damage.

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:03.240
We'll still have LP left.

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:05.780
Only if that's his only move.

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:09.390
Exactly.  I'm not done yet!

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:13.270
Rousing Hydradrive Monarch's 
additional effect!

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:17.730
By removing one Hydradrive 
Counter, I roll a die!

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:26.200
I send all your monsters with the 
corresponding Attribute to the graveyard!

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:31.460
And you take 500 damage for each one.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:32.450
What?

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.660
A strategy based on luck?

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:37.190
That's unlike an AI!

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:40.310
Odds mean luck.

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:46.900
The unpredictability of luck equals 
diversity, opening up new possibilities to dueling.

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:50.670
That's what I've learned 
from my experiences so far!

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:55.410
I accept luck for my future!

00:09:57.960 --> 00:09:59.840
Judgment Dice!

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:20.640
I rolled Dark Attribute!

00:10:21.590 --> 00:10:26.840
So your Cyberse Witch and Cyberse 
Magician are sent to the graveyard!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.040
Is this for real?

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:35.510
You take 500 damage for each 
monster sent to the graveyard!

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:41.630
Now there are no monsters on your field.

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:45.220
Can you survive my attack, Playmaker?

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:46.790
Battle!

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:53.980
The Equip Spell, Resume Mace's effect 
activates from the graveyard!

00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:59.600
Before the battle, I banish two Equip 
Spells and one monster from my graveyard.

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:06.380
Your monster loses ATK equal the original 
ATK of the banished monster this turn!

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:10.820
I banish Resume Mace and Suspend Wand!

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:13.550
And Dotscaper!

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:17.140
Dotscaper has 0 ATK, so 
even if you banish it...

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:20.830
...Rousing Hydradrive Monarch's 
ATK don't decrease.

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:23.290
I know that!

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:26.260
I activate Dotscaper's effect!

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:31.470
Once during a duel, it Special 
Summons itself when it's banished!

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:34.580
He's bringing out a monster 
to shield himself.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:37.410
Rousing Hydradrive Monarch's effect!

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:40.420
As long as this card is 
in the Monster Zone...

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:44.600
...both players can only 
summon monsters with the

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:47.890
same Attribute as this 
card in attack position.

00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:52.210
It has 0 ATK!  This is bad!

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:54.860
I activate Linkuriboh's 
effect from my graveyard!

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:59.130
I tribute a Level 1 monster to Special 
Summon it from the graveyard!

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:05.340
You know Linkuriboh's effect, right?

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:14.200
When your monster attacks, I can tribute 
Linkuriboh to lower its ATK to 0 this turn!

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:18.340
Thanks for your help, Linkuriboh!

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:24.160
Fine.  I end my turn.

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:27.280
That was scary.

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:32.600
But Playmaker...  Since I've 
awakened, can you keep up with me?

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:43.030
My turn!  I draw!

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:46.780
We've been on the back foot this whole duel.

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:50.010
It's clearly my fault.  Sorry.

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:52.080
It's not your fault.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.860
You're just a hostage.

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:56.250
I make the decisions in this duel.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:58.390
What?  That's what you meant?

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:00.020
But I still have a chance.

00:13:00.020 --> 00:13:02.020
I have 550 LP.

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:03.550
Storm Access?

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:05.520
Then you still have a secret weapon.

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:07.500
Look at your Disk.

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:08.970
What's this?

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:14.490
Every since I learned of Cyberse World's 
destruction, I kept building a new program.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:16.870
And I just finished it.

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:19.110
That's remarkable timing.

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:21.800
Okay, I lied.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:24.350
You could've always used 
it, but I kept it secret.

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:26.600
That's more like you.

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:27.680
Mean!

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:32.290
As expected, he'll now...

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.030
Use it.

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:41.670
I activate my Skill!

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:46.440
Neo Storm Access!

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:51.540
Neo Storm Access?

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:53.930
What's that light?

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:59.420
Due to Neo Storm Access, once during the 
duel, when I have 1000 or fewer LP...

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:05.760
...I can add a random Cyberse in 
the Data Storm to my Extra Deck!

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.660
He updated his Skill.

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:20.810
Their instincts led to a new 
possibility.  Interesting.

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:25.310
I activate the Ritual Spell, 
Cynet Ritual from my graveyard!

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.710
When there are no monsters on my field...

00:14:28.710 --> 00:14:36.040
...I can banish this card and a Ritual 
Monster to Special Summon two Cynet Tokens!

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:38.340
In that case...

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.720
No, not yet.

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:45.210
I should observe their new possibility.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:48.530
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:51.430
Link Summon!

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:54.500
Link 2 Cyberse Wicckid!

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:59.970
Then I Special Summon Backup Secretary!

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:06.050
When there's a Cyberse on my field, I can 
Special Summon this monster from my hand!

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:08.400
Cyberse Wicckid's effect!

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:11.760
When a monster is Special 
Summoned next to its link...

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:13.930
... I can banish Dotscaper from my graveyard

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:18.050
to add Cyberse Synchron from my 
deck to my hand and summon it!

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:22.840
Due to Cyberse Synchron's effect,

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:28.980
my Level 4 or lower monster's Level 
increases by its original amount!

00:15:29.270 --> 00:15:34.640
I see.  The new monster you 
instinctively drew is...

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:36.580
But you'll go no further.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:39.770
Rousing Hydradrive Monarch's effect!

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:43.090
Judgment Dice!

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:44.370
What?

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:47.190
You can use that effect during our turn?

00:15:53.570 --> 00:15:55.940
It's Dark Attribute!

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:58.270
No way!  Not again!

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:06.010
All your Dark monsters are sent to the 
graveyard, and you take 500 damage for each one!

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:11.980
Your Dark monsters are Cyberse 
Wicckid and Cyberse Synchron!

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:14.990
You take 1000 damage!  I win!

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:16.580
That won't happen.

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:17.220
What?

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:19.640
Cyberse Wicckid's effect!

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:21.740
Since it was Link Summoned,

00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:25.600
your effects can't affect this monster 
and the Cyberse next to its link!

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:30.470
Yay!  See the power of their bond?

00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:32.830
What an annoying effect.

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:35.170
Cyberse Synchron's effect!

00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:39.880
Backup Secretary's Level increases!

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:46.180
Level 1 Cyberse Synchron tunes 
Level 6 Backup Secretary!

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:00.530
Flash of lightning!

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:04.500
The unknown power transforms 
into a soaring dragon!

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.240
Synchro Summon!

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:12.740
Descend!  Cyberse Quantum Dragon!

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:19.580
This is the power created by their instincts.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:23.780
But that monster has 2500 ATK!

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:26.560
Can you defeat my emperor with that?

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:27.790
Here I go, Bohman!

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:33.600
Cyberse Quantum Dragon attacks 
Rousing Hydradrive Monarch!

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:38.400
What's he thinking?

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:42.200
We can use Judgment Arrows 
to raise its ATK to 6000.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:44.010
He's attacking into that?

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:48.450
Cyberse Quantum Dragon's effect!

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:54.320
When it battles your monster, your 
monster returns to your hand!

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:55.430
What?

00:17:55.430 --> 00:17:57.520
Driveback Shot!

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:06.600
Cyberse Quantum Dragon's additional effect!

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:13.280
When Driveback Shot succeeds, 
Quantum Dragon can attack again!

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:15.970
I attack you directly!

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:18.510
We win!

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:20.500
Take this!  Bing boom bang-

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:22.680
Quantum Encryption!

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:28.260
I can't believe I have to do this.

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:33.950
I activate the Quick-Play Spell, Hydradrive 
Scabbard's effect from my graveyard!

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:38.800
When I'm attacked directly while 
I have Earth, Water, Fire

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:42.260
and Wind Hydradrive Link 
Monsters in my graveyard...

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:48.810
...I can banish this card to halve the 
damage, and we both take that damage!

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:49.810
What?

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:51.780
Half the damage is...

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:55.480
1250!  If they take it...

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:04.450
It's a tie.

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:10.590
Playmaker!  Ai!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:14.070
I've ascertained your powers!

00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:16.300
We will show up again!

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:19.270
We're the nightmare that'll defeat you!

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:23.240
We'll settle this at a new stage!

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:28.920
Why's he acting cool when 
he's the one running away?

00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:33.050
His growth far exceeded my expectations.

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:36.100
Bohman - the evolving AI.

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:39.880
The next time we meet, how strong will he be?

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:42.060
He's a fearsome opponent.

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:46.140
Bohman and Playmaker's signals vanished.

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:48.670
Seems there was no winner.

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:50.300
Wait, Lightning!

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:51.540
We're your opponents!

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:53.130
Before that...

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:56.010
We'll battle you!

00:19:56.810 --> 00:19:58.200
They're escaping!

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:03.630
How dare you interfere!

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:05.100
What should we do with them?

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:08.890
Against these weaklings, we'll 
just be wasting our energy.

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:10.970
Let's do a courageous retreat.

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:12.700
I agree.

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:19.490
Welcome!

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:22.160
I'm glad to see you're safe.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:30.140
Because if you leave the front lines, 
Playmaker's strength will go down greatly.

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:31.530
You're...

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:32.820
Revolver!

00:20:32.820 --> 00:20:34.110
Seriously?

00:20:34.110 --> 00:20:35.810
What do you want?

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:38.490
Craving a hot dog?

00:20:38.490 --> 00:20:41.090
Seems you let Bohman escape.

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:43.050
You sure know a lot.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:46.400
The Hanoi monitors the entire network.

00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:49.300
Same as the Ignis.

00:20:51.760 --> 00:20:53.030
What's this?

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:56.240
A get-well gift, if you will.

00:20:56.240 --> 00:20:58.040
Some kind of program?

00:20:58.040 --> 00:20:59.840
But why give it to us in person?

00:20:59.840 --> 00:21:03.340
They'll notice if I sent it through the net.

00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:06.940
I don't know what they'll try to do.

00:21:07.340 --> 00:21:12.780
They may attack you, similar to 
what they did to Jin Kusanagi.

00:21:12.780 --> 00:21:13.920
Attack us?

00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:17.680
That program will protect you from attacks.

00:21:17.680 --> 00:21:21.790
Once you install it, they can't attack you.

00:21:21.790 --> 00:21:25.370
You expect us to trust a program you built-

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:28.420
Hey!

00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:33.240
Well?

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:35.340
It's an incredible program.

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.390
My business is done.

00:21:39.680 --> 00:21:41.990
Why give it to us?

00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:44.200
We're enemies, right?

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:49.630
The enemy of my enemy is a 
friend... is all I'll say.

00:21:49.630 --> 00:21:50.970
That means...

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:53.120
Survive this fight.

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:56.900
If you survive, then we'll 
settle things between us.

00:22:22.300 --> 00:22:23.800
Trapped in conventionality

00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:25.240
Even denials are obvious

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:26.370
That There This Whichever

00:22:26.370 --> 00:22:28.210
Hey, isn't it true?

00:22:28.540 --> 00:22:29.870
Why is it before you wake up

00:22:29.870 --> 00:22:31.440
You build a wall, saying it's impossible

00:22:31.440 --> 00:22:32.610
No discussions, no ideals

00:22:36.930 --> 00:22:39.650
Even together, it's not the same

00:22:39.950 --> 00:22:42.720
Break yourself through  go way

00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:45.860
Even if you lose your 
way, keep moving forward

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:48.930
Our desires won't be stopped

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:57.500
Let your emotions spill

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:03.640
Keep rewriting  only glory

00:23:04.040 --> 00:23:09.050
If we're together

00:23:09.350 --> 00:23:12.450
We can seize it

00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:40.700
Those who help and those who take.

00:23:41.260 --> 00:23:45.440
The fight for the Water Ignis begins.

00:23:45.660 --> 00:23:53.810
She has the ability to see the truth, 
so what will she see in this battle?

00:23:54.020 --> 00:23:57.480
That voice...  Are you...?

00:23:57.480 --> 00:24:02.190
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Captured Ignis

00:24:02.190 --> 00:24:04.310
Into the VRAINS!
